  "text": "FULafia Library \u2013 Your portal to information! Skip to content library@fulafia.edu.ng Makurdi Road, Lafia, Nasarawa State, Nigeria Search for: Search for: library@fulafia.edu.ng Makurdi Road, Lafia, Nasarawa State, Nigeria Search for: Latest Posts INFORMATION IS POWER May 05, 2024 0 MAXIMIZE THE LIBRARY Apr 04, 2024 0 WHY FULAFIA LIBRARY Mar 03, 2024 0 Education Project FULafia Library Primary Menu Home Resources Subscribed Databases Open Access Databases Online Journals Online Books Intranet Books Law Resources Reference Resources FULafia Webinar FULafia Journals Institutional Repository e-Newspapers Open Educational Resources (OER) Services About Contact LibGuide Log In Start your Search here! Website Search Search OPAC Keyword Title Author Subject ISBN Series Call Number Accession No. Item type Textbooks Reference Books Gifted Books Book Bank Journals & Periodicals Articles Books Search GScholar Repositories Databases E-Journals E-Books Repository E-Learning University Librarian\u2019s Welcome Address Dear Students and Esteemed Colleagues, It is with great pleasure and enthusiasm that I warmly welcome you all to our esteemed Library. As the University Librarian, I am delighted to have this opportunity to address you. The university library serves as the heart of academic life, offering a vast array of resources and services to support your research, learning, and intellectual pursuits. Whether you are here to delve into scholarly texts, access online databases, seek assistance from our knowledgeable staff, or simply find a quiet space to study, our library is here to cater to your needs. I encourage students to make the most of this resource-rich environment. Explore our collection of books, journals, and digital materials to deepen your understanding of your subjects and broaden your horizons. Our library staff is ready to assist you in navigating these resources effectively. To our faculty and researchers, the library is your partner in academic excellence. We are committed to providing you with the resources necessary to support your teaching and research activities. Do not hesitate to reach out to us for personalized assistance or to discuss ways in which we can enhance our services to better serve your needs. Beyond being a repository of knowledge, the library also serves as a hub for intellectual engagement and community building. Prof. Abdulrahman Baba Abdulrazaq University Librarian Ask A Librarian Need help with your research, assignment or using the Library? Ask a Librarian is the general contact point for assistance from FULafia Library Librarians. Ask Now Open Hours Mondays \u2013 Fridays 8:00 AM \u2013 6:00 PM Saturdays -Sundays 10:00 AM \u2013 3:00 PM Online 24 Hrs * The Library is closed on public holidays New Books In Our Collections Quick Links ProQuest Database ProQuest Database\u00a0gives full-text access to thousands of journals covering more than 160 subject areas. Login ProQuest eBooks ProQuest Ebook Central is a collection of electronic books in a wide range of subject areas. Login Ebsco Host EBSCO database provide access to e-books, e-journals and a variety of proprietary full text databases. Login JStore JSTOR provides access to more than 12 million journal articles, books, images, and primary sources in 75 disciplines. Login Intranet Library resources on LAN Open Mendeley Reference manager software Login EagleScan Online plagiarism checking tool Login MS Teams Online Collaboration tool Login Users\u2019 Education Education Project WHY FULAFIA LIBRARY March 4, 2024 The Federal University of Lafia (FULafia) Library stands as a beacon of knowledge and learning, playing an indispensable role\u2026 Education MAXIMIZE THE LIBRARY April 1, 2024 The Federal University of Lafia (FULafia) Library is an invaluable resource for students, staff, and researchers. It provides\u2026 Education INFORMATION IS POWER May 6, 2024 Information is often regarded as a cornerstone of power in the modern world. It shapes decisions, drives progress, and empowe\u2026 Frequently Asked Questions How can I find materials in the Library? Use the Traditional Card catalogue or the Online Public Access Catalogue (OPAC). Each contains materials held by the Library. If you cannot find what you need in the catalogue, please seek assistance at the Circulation Desk. What should I do if I can\u2019t find the book I need on the shelf? Seek assistance at the Circulation Desk or from library personnel in the reading areas if you have difficulties locating a book on the shelf. How can I get a book that is not available in the Library? You may seek assistance of the Reference Librarian if the book you need is unavailable in the library. The library may request to borrow a copy of the item from another library via its Inter-Library Loan Service or purchase it. How do I get login details for subscribed databases? Visit the Library and request for login details from any of the e-librarians on duty. Can I photocopy in the Library\u2019s reading room? Yes. The Library provides photocopying, printing and scanning services. Learn About Us Website Search Search OPAC Keyword Title Author Subject ISBN Series Call Number Accession No. Item type Textbooks Reference Books Gifted Books Book Bank Journals & Periodicals Articles Books Search GScholar Repositries About Vision Mission Core Values Objectives Services Departments University Librarian Strategic Plan Contact Resources Databases e-Journals e-Books Institutional Repository e-Learning Lecture Notes TEEAL LibGuide OPAC My FULafia FULafia Website Staff Mail Staff Portal UG Students Portal PG Students Portal Diploma Portal Prelim/IJMB Portal SIWES Portal CCEDP Portal My Library Library Account Ask A Librarian Staff Login Rules and Regulations Suggest a Purchase Make a Donation Library Tour Feedback FAQs \u00a9 2024 FULafia Library. All rights reserved."
